@@ -533,7 +533,11 @@ When using **Cover**, **Cover + Custom**, or **Cover Overlay**, two more setting

 To use custom sleep images, set the sleep screen to **Custom**, **Cover + Custom**, **Page Overlay**, or **Cover Overlay**, then place images on the SD card:

-- **Multiple Images (recommended):** Create a `.sleep` directory in the root of the SD card and place any number of `.bmp` images inside. In **Page Overlay** and **Cover Overlay** modes, `.png` images are also supported. One image will be randomly selected each time the device sleeps. (A directory named `sleep` is also accepted as a fallback.)
+- **Multiple Images (recommended):** Create a `.sleep` directory in the root of the SD card and place BMP, PNG, JPEG (`.jpg` or `.jpeg`), or GIF images inside for **Custom** and **Cover + Custom** modes. GIFs display their first frame only (up to 480 pixels wide on the device). **Page Overlay** mode supports BMP and PNG. One image will be randomly selected each time the device sleeps. (A directory named `sleep` is also accepted as a fallback.)
+- **Single Image:** In **Custom** mode, place `sleep.bmp`, `sleep.png`, `sleep.jpg`, `sleep.jpeg`, or `sleep.gif` in the root directory. **Page Overlay** supports `sleep.bmp` and `sleep.png`. These files are used as fallbacks if no valid image is found in the `.sleep`/`sleep` directory.
+
+In **Page Overlay** mode, white BMP pixels and transparent PNG pixels let the current reader page show through; the remaining wallpaper pixels are drawn over the page.
+In **Page Overlay** and **Cover Overlay** modes, `.png` images are also supported. One image will be randomly selected each time the device sleeps. (A directory named `sleep` is also accepted as a fallback.)
 - **Single Image:** Place a file named `sleep.bmp` in the root directory. In **Page Overlay** and **Cover Overlay** modes, `sleep.png` is also supported. These files are used as fallbacks if no valid image is found in the `.sleep`/`sleep` directory.

 In **Page Overlay** mode, white BMP pixels and transparent PNG pixels let the current reader page show through; the remaining wallpaper pixels are drawn over the page. **Cover Overlay** uses the same image selection over the current book cover. PNG alpha transparency preserves cover grayscale on supported panels; BMP white pixels are transparent and other pixels form a black mask.
